# What must never reach the image.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so without this file the build context is the
# whole working tree. Two consequences, one merely wasteful and one serious:
#
#   venv/ is 322 MB of host-platform wheels that the image rebuilds anyway from
#   requirements.txt. Copying it inflates the image and can shadow correctly
#   built packages with ones compiled for a different platform.
#
#   .env would be copied in. A credential baked into an image is exposed to
#   anyone who can pull or inspect it, and `docker history` will show it even
#   if a later layer deletes the file. That is the same failure as committing
#   a secret to git, and the project rules are explicit about it.
#
# Everything excluded here is either rebuilt inside the image or has no
# business in a running service.

# Secrets — the important one
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Virtualenvs: rebuilt from requirements.txt inside the image
venv/
.venv/
env/

# Version control and CI
.git/
.github/
.gitignore

# Data extracts. Staging data is mounted or fetched at runtime, never baked in.
data/*.csv
data/*.json
# ...except the committed slice, which is what the deployed service serves.
!data/public/*.csv

# The shipped model, admitted by exact name the same way, and nothing else from
# models/: a stray artefact must not ride into the image. If these three are
# missing the service still starts, on the blend, and /health says so; the
# image check in README.md ("Is the model in the image?") catches that.
models/*
!models/extratrees-v2.joblib
!models/extratrees-v2.manifest.json
!models/extratrees-v2.calibration.json

# Tests and development tooling: the image runs the service, it does not test it.
# CI runs the suite against the source, which is the right place for it.
tests/
scripts/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Python build artefacts. The **/ matters: a bare `__pycache__/` matches only
# at the root of the build context, which let the host's app/__pycache__/ into
# the image until a `find` inside the container showed it.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Documentation — useful in the repo, dead weight in a container
*.md
!README.md

# The Flutter client. It is built and served separately; the service image
# has no use for a Dart project, its build output or its Android tree.
client/

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
